  <glossary>
      <definition id="def-00001">
        <term>Finite Population Correction Factor</term>
        <meaning>a factor, <m:math><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>N</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi>N</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:math>, used to adjust the variance (and thus the standard deviation) of a sampling distribution when more than 5% of a finite population of known size <m:math><m:mi>N</m:mi></m:math> is sampled.</meaning>
      </definition>
  </glossary>
</document>
